    <h2>FAQ</h2>

    <h3>Is the CalDigit TS4 better than the Satechi Thunderbolt 4 Dock?</h3>
    <p>The CalDigit TS4 is better for power users who need the maximum port count (18 ports), 98W power delivery, and the most refined firmware and thermal performance. The Satechi Thunderbolt 4 Dock is better for buyers who want a more affordable, compact dock that still drives dual 4K displays at 60Hz and delivers 96W of charging in a sleek aluminum design.</p>

    <h3>Can the CalDigit TS4 and Satechi Thunderbolt 4 Dock drive two 4K displays?</h3>
    <p>Yes, both docks support dual 4K displays at 60Hz over Thunderbolt 4, provided your host computer has a Thunderbolt 4 port and the displays connect via Thunderbolt or DisplayPort. The CalDigit TS4 additionally supports a single 8K display, which the Satechi dock does not.</p>

    <h3>Which Thunderbolt 4 dock is better for Mac, the CalDigit TS4 or the Satechi?</h3>
    <p>Both are fully compatible with Mac and Windows. The CalDigit TS4 has a longer track record of firmware stability on macOS and is widely regarded as the most reliable Thunderbolt 4 dock for Mac users. The Satechi dock is also Mac-compatible and its aluminum design matches Apple aesthetics, but some users report occasional firmware quirks that CalDigit resolves more quickly.</p>

    <h3>What is the difference in power delivery between the CalDigit TS4 and Satechi dock?</h3>
    <p>The CalDigit TS4 delivers 98W of power to the host laptop, while the Satechi Thunderbolt 4 Dock delivers 96W. Both are sufficient to fast-charge any modern MacBook or Windows laptop under full load, including the 16-inch MacBook Pro. The 2W difference is negligible in practice and does not affect charging performance for any current laptop.</p>

    <h3>Do both docks support ethernet, and what speeds?</h3>
    <p>Yes, both docks include ethernet, but speeds differ. The CalDigit TS4 includes 2.5GbE ethernet, which is 2.5 times faster than standard gigabit ethernet and benefits users on high-speed networks or NAS setups. The Satechi Thunderbolt 4 Dock includes 1GbE ethernet, which is adequate for most home and office networks but slower than the TS4's 2.5GbE.</p>

    <h3>Can I use the CalDigit TS4 or Satechi dock with a USB-C only laptop?</h3>
    <p>Both docks require a Thunderbolt 4 or Thunderbolt 3 port on the host laptop to deliver full functionality, including dual display support and maximum bandwidth. A USB-C only port without Thunderbolt will not work with either dock. Check your laptop's specifications to confirm it has a Thunderbolt 4 or Thunderbolt 3 port before purchasing either dock.</p>

